# Keyword reference from the user (Keywords 4_14_22 doc). Evergreen and expansion keywords are merged into kind=keyword (evergreen distinction ignored, user 2026-10-22). Summaries are the doc's plain-language wording (first two points), not rules text: a few are inexact (e.g. Bolster, Renown, Fabricate); check Forge script / Oracle text before relying on one. ability_word entries (Landfall, Raid...) are flavour labels, not Forge K: keywords.
keywords[172]{name,kind,example,summary}:
  Deathtouch,keyword,Sedge Scorpion,"Whenever a creature with deathtouch deals damage to another creature, that creature will die. It does not have to be combat damage, so if you have a card like Rabid Bite, it will still kill the creature dealt damage."
  Defender,keyword,Wall of Mist,"Creature cannot attack. In the past, there was a rule that said \"Walls can't attack.\" So if you see an old creature with the type \"Wall\", but it doesn't have defender in the text-box, it still has defender."
  Double Strike,keyword,Boros Swiftblade,Creature deals both first strike damage and regular damage.
  Enchant,keyword,Abundant Growth,"Written as \"Enchant X\" where X is a permanent type These are auras."
  Equip,keyword,Sword of Feast and Famine,"Written as \"Equip X\" where X is a mana cost These are equipment."
  First Strike,keyword,Battle Hurda,"Creature with first strike deals damage before creatures without first strike in combat. For example, if you have a 2/2 elf and a 2/2 soldier with first strike in combat, the elf would die before it deals damage to the soldier."
  Flash,keyword,Bounding Krasis,"This is on nonland permanent cards (creatures, artifact, enchantments, planeswalkers). Permits you to cast those spells whenever you could cast an instant."
  Flying,keyword,Storm Crow,Creatures with flying can only be blocked by other creatures with flying or by creatures with reach.
  Haste,keyword,Tenement Crasher,"Creatures with haste may attack or activate \"tap\" abilities the turn they come into play, i.e. no summoning sickness."
  Lifelink,keyword,Bishop's Soldier,"Whenever a creature with lifelink deals damage, either to an opponent or creature, you gain life equal to the amount of damage. All damage happens at the same time. If you are dealt lethal damage, but have a lifelink creature to block that brings you back up a"
  Menace,keyword,Ruin Grinder,"Creatures with menace can only be blocked by 2 or more creatures. When paired with deathtouch, it's very potent."
  Protection,keyword,Apostle of Purifying Light,"Written as \"Protection from X\" This is complicated."
  Prowess,keyword,Monastery Swiftspear,"Whenever you cast a noncreature spell, prowess creatures get +1/+1 until end of turn. Does stack, so if you cast 2 noncreature spells, prowess creatures get +1/+1 for each of those spells, getting +2/+2 total."
  Reach,keyword,Giant Spider,Creatures with reach may block creatures with flying.
  Trample,keyword,Colossal Dreadmaw,Creatures with trample deal excess damage to defending player. Example
  Vigilance,keyword,Serra Angel,Attacking does not cause creature to tap.
  Ward,keyword,Dreadlight Monstrosity,"Written as \"Ward [cost]\" If a creature with ward becomes the target of a spell or ability an opponent controls, counter that spell unless the opponent pays the ward cost."
  Attach,action,"","Used on auras, equipment, and fortifications (only one fortification, Darksteel Garrison, in the game.) Used to \"put on\" an aura or equipment to a permanent."
  Clash,action,Fire Juggler,"When a spell tells players to clash, each player reveals the top card of their library. When they do, the person with the higher mana value of the revealed card wins the clash. In the event of a tie, there is no winner."
  Counter,action,Counterspell,"Countering a spell or ability removes it from the stack. Also called permission, because you get to say \"no\" to so many things."
  Reconfigure,action,The Reality Chip,"Written as \"Reconfigure X\" where X is a mana cost These are artifact creatures that are also equipment."
  Regeneration,action,Ancient Silverback,"Written as \"regenerate: [cost]\" When the regeneration cost is paid, it gives that permanent a \"regeneration shield\" for the rest of the turn."
  Sacrifice,action,Chainer's Edict,"The owner of a permanent places it into their own graveyard due to an effect or spell. Some spells cause you to sacrifice a creature as an additional cost, sometimes spells an opponent cast can cause you to sacrifice a creature."
  Scry,action,Crystal Ball,"Written as \"Scry X\" where X is a number Look at the top X cards of your library, put any number on the bottom of your library. Put the rest back in any order."
  Tap/untap,action,"",Allows you to tap or untap a permanent.
  Absorb,keyword,"","Only on one card: Lymph Sliver Written as \"Absorb X\" where X is a number"
  Adapt,keyword,Growth-Chamber Guardian,"Written as \"[cost] Adapt X\", where X is a number When the adapt cost is paid, put X +1/+1 counters on the creatures whose ability was activated."
  Adventure,keyword,Bonecrusher Giant,"On a card with adventure, you may cast a spell for it's adventure cost. If you do, exile that card. You may then cast the creature side from exile. You have to cast adventure spell, then creature half. You cannot cast creature half, then adventure from exile."
  Affinity,keyword,Thoughtcast,"Written as \"Affinity for X\", where X is a card type Most commonly written as \"affinity for artifacts\", a card can have affinity for anything."
  Afterlife,keyword,Orzhov Enforcer,"Written as \"Afterlife X\", where X is an number When a creature with afterlife dies, it's controller creates X 1/1 black and white spirit tokens with flying equal to the afterlife number."
  Aftermath,keyword,Commit to Memory,"Only on split cards One side may only be cast from your hand, the other side may only be cast from the graveyard."
  Alliance,keyword,Gala Greeters,"Basically \"Landfall\", but on creatures. Whenever another creature enters, some effect happens."
  Amplify,keyword,Kilnmouth Dragon,"Written as \"Amplify X\", where X is a number When you cast a card with amplify, you may reveal any number of cards that share a card type with that card. The card that was cast then enters with a number of +1/+1 counters equal to X times the amount of cards rev"
  Annihilator,keyword,Ulamog's Crusher,"Written as \"Annihilator X\", where X is a number Whenever a creature with annihilator attacks, the defending player sacrifices X permanents, where X is the number associated with annihilator."
  Aura Swap,keyword,Arcanum Wings,"Written as \"Aura Swap X\", where X is a mana cost When a card with aura swap is attached to a creature, you may pay the cost associated with aura swap to return the attached card to your hand and attach an aura from your hand to the same creature."
  Banding,keyword,Knights of Thorn,"Historically, THE MOST complicated mechanic in all of MTG history. 53 words of rules text:"
  Battle Cry,keyword,Signal Pest,"Whenever a creature with battle cry attacks, other attacking creatures get +1/+0 until the end of turn."
  Bestow,keyword,Celestial Archon,"Written as \"Bestow [cost]\" When you pay the bestow cost, you use a creature with bestow as an aura for a creature on the battlefield. If the bestowed creature dies, the creature with bestow stays on the battlefield."
  Blitz,keyword,"","Written as \"Blitz [cost]\" You may cast a card for it's blitz cost. If you do, it gains haste. Sacrifice it at the next end step and draw a card."
  Bloodrush,keyword,Skarrg Goliath,"Written as \"Bloodrush [cost]\" You may discard a creature with bloodrush by paying its bloodrush cost. Then, a target creature is granted a boost and abilities based off the discarded creature."
  Bloodthirst,keyword,Scab-Clan Mauler,"Written as \"Bloodthirst X\", where X is a number Creatures with Bloodthirst counters enter the battlefield with X +1/+1 counters on them, if an opponent was dealt damage this turn."
  Bolster,keyword,"Dromoka, the Eternal","Written as \"Bolster X\", where X is a number Whenever a creature with bolster attacks, you put X +1/+1 counters on target creature you control with the lowest toughness equal to the X in bolster."
  Bushido,keyword,Devoted Retainer,"Written as \"Bushido X\", where X is a number If a creature with Bushido is blocked or blocks, it gets +X/+X until the end of the turn, where X is the number associated with Bushido."
  Buyback,keyword,Capsize,"Written as \"Buyback X\", where X is a mana cost. Only on instants and sorceries. When you cast a card, you may pay the buyback cost. If you do, instead of the card going to your graveyard, it goes back to your hand after resolving."
  Cascade,keyword,Bloodbraid Elf,"Whenever a you cast a card with cascade, exile the top card of your library until you find a card with a lesser converted mana cost, then you may cast that card without paying its mana cost. 2 spells for the cost of 1 spell. Very powerful, considered broken."
  Casualty,keyword,A Little Chat,"Written as \"Casualty X\", where X is a number When you cast a card with casualty, you may sacrifice a creature with power equal to the X value. If you do, copy the spell."
  Champion,keyword,Wanderwine Prophets,"Written as \"Champion a [creature type]\" When you cast a creature with champion, you must exile a card that is the type referred to in the champion keyword. If the champion card leaves play, the exiled card will be returned to the battlefield."
  Changeling,keyword,Chameleon Colossus,"Creatures with changeling count as all creature types, therefore benefitting from all bonuses associated with tribal synergies. Very common in decks without many good creatures of a specific type."
  Channel,keyword,Greater Tanuki,"Written as \"Channel [cost]\" You may pay the channel cost of a card in your hand, if you do, you discard that card and yield some effect."
  Cipher,keyword,Call of the Nightwing,"When you cast a spell with cipher, you may exile it as it resolves. Then, choose a creature to \"cipher\" the spell onto. Whenever that creature deals damage to an opponent, you may cast the \"ciphered\" spell without paying its cost. Sounds really strong, but usu"
  Connive,keyword,Ledger Shredder,"Written as \"[CARDNAME] connives\" Whenever a card connives, you draw and discard a card. If a nonland card was discarded this way, put a +1/+1 counter on the creature that connived."
  Conspire,keyword,Giantbaiting,"Only on instants and sorceries. When you cast a spell with conspire, you may tap 2 creatures that share a color with the spell. If you do, copy that spell."
  Convoke,keyword,March of the Multitudes,"Convoke allows you to tap creatures to pay for the cost in a spell. Creatures tapped with convoke can either pay for generic costs or colored costs, as long as they are the same color as the mana symbol they are paying."
  Coven,keyword,Augur of Autumn,"If you control at least 3 creatures with different powers, then creatures with coven gain some benefit."
  Crew,keyword,Aethersphere Harvester,"Written as \"Crew X\" where X is a number Only on vehicles. To crew a vehicle, you must tap any number of creatures whos power equals X or greater."
  Cumulative Upkeep,keyword,Mystic Remora,"Written as \"Cumulative Upkeep [cost]\" Old and difficult mechanic. Essentially, the cost compounds each turn, and must be paid at the upkeep step. On your upkeep you place an age-counter on the card with cumulative upkeep, then pay the upkeep cost as many times"
  Cycling,keyword,Cast Out,"Written as \"Cycling [cost] Whenever a card has cycling, you may pay the cycling cost and discard that card. Then you draw a new card."
  Dash,keyword,"Ragavan, Nimble Pilferer","You may pay the dash cost for a creature, that creature gains haste and returns to your hand at the end of the turn. Helps you dodge sorcery speed removal spells, like board sweepers."
  Daybound/Nightbound,keyword,Brutal Cathar,"The day/night cycle must be introduced by a card with daybound/nightbound. Whenever a player plays 2 or more spells on their turn, it becomes day. If a player casts no spells during their turn, it becomes night. Cards with this mechanic transform or give some"
  Delve,keyword,Treasure Cruise,"Delve allows you to exile cards from your graveyard to pay the generic mana cost of the card with delve. For example, with Treasure Cruise if you have 12 cards in your graveyard, you may pay 1 blue mana and \"delve\" 7 cards to draw 3 cards while only paying 1 m"
  Detain,keyword,Lavinia of the Tenth,"Whenever a player \"detains\" a permanent, that permanent cannot attack, block, or activate abilities until the start of that player's next turn."
  Devour,keyword,Predator Dragon,"Written as \"Devour X\", where X is a number Whenever a creature with devour enters the battlefield, you may sacrifice any number of creatures you control. The creature with devour then gets X +1/+1 counters for each creature sacrificed this way."
  Disturb,keyword,Lunarch Veteran,"Written as \"Disturb [cost]\" Whenever a card with disturb is in your graveyard, you may cast it for its disturb cost. When you do, it enters the battlefield transformed."
  Dredge,keyword,Life from the Loam,"Written as \"Dredge X\", where X is a number If a card with dredge is in your graveyard, instead of drawing a card, you may put the top X cards of your library into your graveyard where X number associated with the ability, and return the dredge card to your han"
  Echo,keyword,Avalanche Riders,"Written as \"Echo [cost]\" Whenever a card with echo comes into play under your control, you must pay the echo cost at the beginning of the next upkeep or sacrifice the creature."
  Embalm,keyword,Aven Wind Guide,"Written as \"Embalm [cost]\" When a creature is in the graveyard, you may pay the embalm cost to exile that creature from your graveyard and make a token of it."
  Emerge,keyword,"",Emerge allows you to sacrifice a creature and pay the difference between the sacrificed creature's mana cost and the emerge cost. Very similar to offering mechanic in that way.
  Entwine,keyword,Tooth and Nail,"Written as \"Entwine [cost]\" On cards with 2 options, it allows you to pay mana in addition to the casting cost to do both options."
  Epic,keyword,Enduring Ideal,"After a card with Epic resolves, you may no longer cast spells. Instead, it provides you with (typically), some insane benefit."
  Escape,keyword,Cling to Dust,"Written as \"Escape [cost]\" You may cast a card from the graveyard for it's escape cost by exiling a specified amount of other cards from your graveyard."
  Evoke,keyword,Mulldrifter,"You may cast a card for its evoke cost, but when it enters the battlefield, it is immediately sacrificed. The evoke cost is usually much less than the cost of casting the card."
  Evolve,keyword,Experiment One,"Whenever a creature with power or toughness greater than a creature with evolve enters the battlefield, put a +1/+1 counter on the creature with evolve. If you play Experiment One on turn 1, then Watchwolf on turn 2, Experiment One will have a +1/+1 counter pu"
  Exalted,keyword,Noble Hierarch,"Whenever a creature you control attacks alone, it gets +1/+1 for each instance of exalted. If you have 2 creatures with exalted, and one of them attacks alone, that is 2 instances of exalted, so that creatures ends up getting +2/+2."
  Exert,keyword,Glorybringer,"When a creature with exert attacks, you may \"exert\" the card. If you do, it does not untap during its controller's next untap step. Cards grant some ability when you exert them."
  Exploit,keyword,Fell Stinger,"Whenever you cast a card with exploit, as an additional cost, you may sacrifice a creature. If you do, you gain some benefit."
  Explore,keyword,Merfolk Branchwalker,"Whenever a creature with explore enters the battlefield, reveal the top card of your library. If it is a land card, put it into your hand. If it is a nonland card, you may put it into your graveyard. For each nonland card revealed this way, put a +1/+1 counter"
  Extort,keyword,Blind Obedience,"Whenever you cast a spell you may pay either white or black mana. If you do, each opponent loses 1 life and you gain life equal to the amount of life lost this way. Because the white mana symbol on extort cards is in the reminder text, extort cards can be play"
  Fabricated,keyword,Angel of Invention,"Written as \"Fabricate X\", where X is a number Whenever a creature with fabricate enters the battlefield, you may either put X +1/+1 counters on that creature or create X 1/1 colorless servo creature tokens."
  Fading,keyword,Tangle Wire,"Written as \"Fading X\", where X is a number Cards with fading enter the battlefield with X fading counters on them. At the beginning of your upkeep, remove a fading counter from that permanent. If you cannot remove a fading counter, sacrifice that creature."
  Fateseal,keyword,Spin into myth,"When you \"scry\" on your opponents' library. You are allowed to look at the top X cards of the opponent's library, as dictated by the number in the keyword. You then decide what stays on top of the library and what goes to the bottom."
  Fear,keyword,Dross Prowler,Only on black cards. The creature that has fear cannot be blocked except by black and artifact creatures.
  Flanking,keyword,Benalish Cavalry,"Whenever a creature with flanking is blocked, the blocking creature gets -1/-1 until the end of the turn. Older mechanic; rare and not all that good."
  Flashback,keyword,Faithless Looting,"Written as \"Flashback [cost]\" When a card with flashback is in the graveyard, you may cast it for its flashback cost, then exile it."
  Flip,keyword,"Erayo, Soratami Ascendant","Flip cards are turned upside-down when a certain condition is met. They are not turned face-down, but rotated 180 degrees."
  Forecast,keyword,Proclamation of Rebirth,"Written as \"Forecast [cost]\" During your upkeep, you may pay the forecast cost and reveal the forecast card from your hand, then the ability from forecast resolves."
  Foretell,keyword,Doomskar,"Written as \"Foretell [cost]\" During your turn, at any time, you may pay 2 to \"foretell\" a card. You may cast that card for its foretell cost on a later turn."
  Frenzy,keyword,Frenzy Sliver,"Written as \"Frenzy X\" where X is a number Whenever a creature with frenzy attacks and isn't blocked, it gets +X/+0 until the end of turn."
  Graft,keyword,Plaxcaster Frogling,"Written as \"Graft X\" where X is a number All creatures with graft are 0/0s that enter the battlefield with X +1/+1 counters on them equal to the graft number. Whenever another creature enters the battlefield, creatures with graft may move one of their counters"
  Gravestorm,keyword,Bitter Ordeal,"When the spell is cast, copy it for each permanent that entered the graveyard this turn. Only on one card with the mechanic."
  Haunt,keyword,Belfry Spirit,"Once a creature or spell with haunt enters the graveyard, it is exiled and then attached to a creature on the battlefield to \"haunt it\". All cards with the haunt mechanic have an enter the battlefield trigger that is the same as the haunt trigger. The haunt tr"
  Hideaway,keyword,Mosswort Bridge,"When a card with hideaway enters the battlefield, you look at the top 4 cards of your library. Exile one card under the hideaway permanent. Then, when a condition is met, you cast the exiled card without paying its mana cost. Only on 5 cards from a set called"
  Horsemanship,keyword,"Sun Quan, Lord of Wu","Horsemanship is like flying. Creatures with horsemanship can't be blocked by creatures without horsemanship, unless explicitly stated otherwise. Only from an old set called Portal: 3 Kingdoms. Set in the 3 Kingdoms era in China. Was originally meant to try to"
  Imprint,keyword,Extraplanar Lens,"Written as \"Imprint [something]\" When a card with imprint enters the battlefield, it can have you exile almost anything, then gives you some boon based on that."
  Indestructible,keyword,"Avacyn, Angle of Hope","Creatures with indestructible cannot be removed from the battlefield by effects that say \"destroy\" nor damage. You can remove indestructible creatures and permanents by exile effects (Swords to Plowshares), -1/-1 effects (Toxic Deluge), and bounce effects (Cyc"
  Inspired,keyword,"King Macar, the Gold-Cursed","Whenever a card with inspired becomes untapped, something happens."
  Investigate,keyword,Thraben Inspector,"Whenever a card investigates, create a clue tokens. Clue tokens have \"Pay 2 mana and sacrifice this artifact, draw a card.\""
  Jump-start,keyword,Radical Idea,Cards with Jump-start may be cast from the graveyard by paying their mana cost and discarding a card.
  Kicker,keyword,"Tourach, Dread Cantor","Written as \"Kicker [cost]\" When you cast a spell, you may also pay the kicker cost to have an additional effect happen."
  Level up,keyword,Lighthouse Chronologist,"Cards with level up enter the battlefield at level 0. You may pay the level up cost to put a level counter on that creature. As creatures \"gain experience (level up)\", they gain more abilities. You may only level up as a sorcery, but may do so as many times as"
  Landwalk,keyword,Benthic Behemoth,"Written as \"plainswalk\" or \"islandwalk\",etc Creatures with landwalk cannot be blocked if the defending player has a land that is the type mentioned in the ability."
  Living Weapon,keyword,Batterskull,"Cards with living weapon are equipment. When they enter the battlefield, they generate a 0/0 black germ creature token, and attach themselves to that creature. Since the germs have no abilities and are 0/0 creatures, they will die if the equipment becomes unat"
  Madness,keyword,Basking Rootwalla,"Written as \"Madness [cost]\" When a spell with madness is discarded, it is exiled. Then, you may cast that card for it's madness cost. If you don't cast it, it is then moved to the graveyard."
  Manifest,keyword,Reality Shift,"Written as \"Manifest [one or more cards]\" Manifested cards are face-down 2/2 creatures, just like morphs. Manifested creatures may be turned face up for their mana cost."
  Meld,keyword,"Brisela, Voice of Nightmares","2 cards can be melded together to create a single creature. Only in one set, not many cards."
  Mentor,keyword,Legion Warboss,"Whenever a card with mentor attacks, put a +1/+1 counter on target attacking creature with less power than the mentor creature. If for some reason, a mentor card is put into the battlefield attacking, it does not trigger mentor. The act of declaring it as an a"
  Miracle,keyword,Temporal Mastery,"You may cast a card for its miracle cost if it is the first card you draw in a turn. Since the timing on miracles is different, if you draw a sorcery on an opponent's turn and it has miracle, you may cast it for its miracle cost, even though it is a sorcery."
  Modular,keyword,Arcbound Mouser,"Written as \"Modular X\", where X is a number Creatures with modular enter with X +1/+1 counters. When a creature with modular dies, it's counters may be moved to another target artifact creature."
  Monstrosity,keyword,Fleecemane Lion,"Written as \"[cost]: Monstrosity X\", where X is a number As long as a card has not already become monstrous, you may pay the monstrosity cost and put X +1/+1 counters on that creature."
  Morph and Megamorph,keyword,Ainok Survivalist,"Written as \"Morph [cost]\" You may pay 3 generic mana and put a card with morph onto the battlefield face down as a colorless 2/2 creature. Then you may pay the morph cost to flip the card face up."
  Mutate,keyword,Dirge Bat,"Written as \"Mutate [cost]\" Creatures may be cast for their mutate cost if targeting a non-human creature you control to mutate onto."
  Ninjutsu,keyword,Ninja of the Deep Hours,"Written as \"Ninjutsu [cost]\" You may return an unblocked attacking creature you control and put a ninja down in its' place, attacking."
  Offering,keyword,Patron of the Kitsune,"Written as \"[creature type] offering\" Creatures with offering may be cast as though it has flash if you sacrifice a creature of the appropriate type. Also, the mana cost is altered based on what you sacrifice. For example, Patron of the Orochi has snake offeri"
  Overload,keyword,Vandalblast,"Written as \"Overload [cost]\" When an instant or sorcery is overloaded, instead of targeting 1 target, it affects all targets."
  Persist,keyword,Kitchen Finks,"If a creature with persist is put into a graveyard from play and had no -1/-1 counters on it, return it to the battlefield with a -1/-1 counter. Doubles up enter the battlefield triggers and death triggers and stuff."
  Phasing,keyword,Sandbar Crocodile,"Old and complicated mechanic Cards that are phased out are treated as though they don't exist. Any auras and equipment attached do not fall off and are phased out with the creature. It's similar to exile, but the creatures return at the beginning of their cont"
  Poisonous,keyword,Virulent Sliver,"Written as \"Poisonous X\", where X is a number Whenever a creature with poisonous deals damage to a player, that player gets X poison counters, where X is the number associated with the ability. If a player has 10 poison counters, they lose the game."
  Populate,keyword,Growing Ranks,Make a copy of a creature token you control.
  Proliferate,keyword,Grateful Apparition,"Whenever you proliferate, you may add an additional counter to anything that already has a counter. This includes +1/+1 counters, loyalty counters, poison counters, etc. Basically all counters."
  Provoke,keyword,Lowland Tracker,"When a creature with provoke attacks, its controller may target a creature defending player controls. Then, untap that creature (if applicable). That creature must block the attacking creature with provoke. They mostly suck in general."
  Prowl,keyword,Latchkey Faerie,"Written as \"Prowl [cost]\" A creature may be cast for its prowl cost, only if a creature that shares a creature type dealt damage to a player this turn."
  Rampage,keyword,Craw Giant,"Written as \"Rampage X\", where X is a number. Whenever a creature with rampage is blocked, it gets +X/+X until end of turn for each creature blocking it."
  Rebound,keyword,Ephemerate,"Whenever you cast a card with rebound, exile it. You may cast that card again without paying its mana cost on your next upkeep."
  Recover,keyword,Icefall,"Written as \"Recover [cost]\" Whenever a creature is put into a player's graveyard from the battlefield, all cards with recover trigger. You may then pay the recover cost for each card and return it to your hand. If you do not or cannot pay the cost, the card is"
  Reinforce,keyword,Burrenton Bombardier,"Written as \"Reinforce: X - [cost]\", where X is a number You may discard a card with reinforce from your hand and pay the reinforce cost, then put X +1/+1 counters on target creature"
  Renown,keyword,Scab-Clan Berserker,"Written as \"Reinforce X\", where X is a number. Whenever a creature with renown deals combat damage to a player for the first time, put X +1/+1 counters on it. It then becomes renown."
  Replicate,keyword,Shattering Spree,"Written as \"Replicate [cost]\" Whenever you cast a spell, you may pay its replicate cost any number of times. If you do, copy that spell for each time you paid the replicate cost."
  Retrace,keyword,Oona's Grace,"Cards with retrace may be cast from the graveyard if you discard a land card in addition to paying their other costs. Unlike most other versions of this, they are not exiled once cast from the graveyard, so you can keep retracing them as long as you have lands"
  Riot,keyword,Gruul Spellbreaker,"Whenever a creature with riot enters the battlefield, its controller chooses for it to enter with either a +1/+1 counter and haste."
  Ripple,keyword,Surging Dementia,"Written as \"Ripple X\", where X is a number When a spell is cast with Ripple, its controller may reveal the top X cards of their library and cast any copies of that card without paying the mana cost. This triggers ripple again."
  Scavenge,keyword,Deadbridge Goliath,"Written as \"Scavenge [cost]\" You may exile a card with scavenge from your graveyard by paying it's scavenge cost. Then, place a number of +1/+1 counters on target creature."
  Shadow,keyword,Dauthi Cutthroat,Creatures with shadow can only block or be blocked by other creatures with shadow.
  Shroud,keyword,Argothian Enchantress,Creatures with shroud cannot be the target of spells or abilities. That includes all players.
  Soulbond,keyword,Deadeye Navigator,Creatures with souldbond enter the battlefield and bond to another creature. Both creatures then gain some boon.
  Soulshift,keyword,Elder Pine of Jukai,"Written as \"Soulshift X\", where X is a number Whenever a creature with soulshift is put into the graveyard, its controller may return a spirit card from the graveyard to their hand with mana value X or less."
  Spectacle,keyword,Light up the Stage,"Written as \"Spectacle [cost]\" You may cast a card for its spectacle cost if an opponent was dealt damage this turn."
  Splice,keyword,Everdream,"Written as \"Splice onto X\", where X is a card type When you cast a card of the specified type, you may pay the splice cost and reveal that card. The effect of the revealed card is then \"tacked onto\" the spell being cast."
  Split Second,keyword,Angel's Grace,"A card with split second cannot be interacted with. Once it is on the stack, nothing else can be put there until it has resolved."
  Storm,keyword,Grapeshot,"Whenever a card with storm is cast, copy it for each spell cast before it this turn. For example, if you cast 2 lightning bolts and then a Grapeshot, there are actually 3 copies of grapeshot because it is copied 2 times from the 2 lightning bolts cast before i"
  Sunburst,keyword,Engineered Explosives,"A card with sunburst enters with a counter on it for each color of mana used to cast the spell. If a card with sunburst cost 5 generic mana, and you spend 3 green mana and 2 black mana, it only gets 2 counters. If you spend one of every color of mana, it gets"
  Support,keyword,Generous Patron,"Written as \"Support X\", where X is a number When the ability resolves, place a +1/+1 counter on up to X target creatures."
  Surveil,keyword,Notion Rain,"Written as \"Surveil X\", where X is a number When the ability resolves, look at the top X cards of your library. You may put any number into your graveyard and rest back on top of your library in any order."
  Suspend,keyword,Rift Bolt,"Written as \"Suspend X [cost]\", where X is a number You may pay the suspend cost for a card and exile it with X time counters on it. At the beginning of your upkeep, remove a time counter from the card. When the last time counter is removed, you may then cast t"
  Totem Armor,keyword,Bear Umbra,"Totem Armor is only on auras. If a creature attached with an aura that has Totem Armor would die, instead, the aura is destroyed instead."
  Transfigure,keyword,Fleshwrither,"Written as \"Transfigure [cost]\" Any time a sorcery could be cast, you may pay the transfigure cost and sacrifice the creature with transfigure to search your library for a creature with the same mana value."
  Transform,keyword,Aberrant Researcher // Perfected Form,"Applies to double-faced cards. When some condition is met, you may transform a card from its front side to its back side. What causes a transformation varies widely from in-game actions to mana costs."
  Transmute,keyword,Muddle the Mixture,"Written as \"Transmute [cost]\" When you transmute a card, you pay the transmute cost and discard that card, then search your library for a card with the same mana value."
  Tribute,keyword,Fanatic of Xenagos,"Written as \"Tribute X\", where X is a number. Whenever a creature with tribute enters the battlefield, an opponent may pay \"tribute\" by putting X +1/+1 counters on it. If the tribute is not paid, some other effect will occur."
  Undying,keyword,Young Wolf,"When a creature with undying is put into the graveyard, if it had no +1/+1 counters, return it to the battlefield with a +1/+1 counter. Yes, this is persist with +1 counters instead of -1 counters."
  Unearth,keyword,Dregscape Zombie,"Written as \"Unearth [cost]\" When a creature with unearth is in the graveyard, you may pay the unearth cost any time you could play a sorcery. Return that creature to the battlefield, and it gains haste. Exile it at the end step."
  Unleash,keyword,Rakdos Cackler,"When a creature with unleash enters the battlefield, its controller may choose to have it enter with a +1/+1 counter on it. If a creature with unleash has a counter on it, it cannot block. The counter does not have to come from unleash, it's any +1/+1 counter."
  Wither,keyword,Harvest Gwyllion,"Wither is a replacement effect. If a creature would be dealt nonlethal damage by a creature with wither, it instead has -1/-1 counters placed on it instead of marking normal damage. This is similar to infect, but players do not receive poison counters from cre"
  Addendum,ability_word,Emergency Powers,Cards with addendum have an added effect if cast in your main phase.
  Battalion,ability_word,Legion Loyalist,Creatures with battalion have an additional effect trigger if they attack with at least 2 other creatures
  Chroma,ability_word,Fiery Bombardment,"Cards with chroma check for specific mana symbols in specific zones, then give a benefit or effect based on that."
  Domain,ability_word,Prismatic Geoscope,"Cards with domain have some effect related to the number of basic land types you control. Some good effects, some bad effects."
  Enrage,ability_word,Ranging Raptors,"Only on creatures. If a creature with enrage is dealt damage, some type of trigger will occur."
  Fateful Hour,ability_word,Break of Day,Cards with fateful hour gain an additional ability if it's controller is at 5 or less life.
  Ferocious,ability_word,Wild Slash,Cards with ferocious gain an additional ability if their controller also controls a creature with more than 4 power.
  Grandeur,ability_word,"Baru, Fist of Krosa",Very few cards with this and they are bad. Allows you to discard a card with the same name to give it a bonus.
  Hellbent,ability_word,Infernal Tutor,"Cards with hellbent give some additional boon or greater effect if you have no cards in hand when the card resolves. If you cast the card, and while it is on the stack, you somehow discard your hand, you will still get the hellbent ability even though you had"
  Heroic,ability_word,Fabled Hero,Cards with heroic grant some additional benefit when targeted with a spell.
  Join forces,ability_word,Collective Voyage,Cards with join forces allow all players to contribute mana towards some effect. Meant for commander/multiplayer games.
  Kinship,ability_word,Pyroclast Consul,"On your upkeep, if you control a card with kinship, you may look at the top card of your library. If it is a creature that shares a type with the kinship creature on the battlefield, you may reveal it for some effect."
  Landfall,ability_word,Khalni Heart Expedition,Cards with landfall have some ability that triggers when a land enters the battlefield.
  Metalcraft,ability_word,Puresteel Paladin,Cards with metalcraft gain an additional benefit if it's controller controls 3 or more artifacts.
  Morbid,ability_word,Tragic Slip,Cards with morbid gain some effect if a creature died that turn.
  Radiance,ability_word,Rally the Righteous,"Basically, if you target a permanent with a spell, that spell affects all permanents of the same type that share a color. If you have 5 white creatures and cast Rally the Righteous on one, the other 4 with also get +3/+3"
  Raid,ability_word,Bloodsoaked Champion,Cards with raid get some effect if their controller attacked before playing them.
  Rally,ability_word,Lantern Scout,Cards with rally have some effect trigger whenever a creature with the type Ally enters the battlefield.
  Sweep,ability_word,Charge Across the Araba,"When you cast a spell with sweep, you may return any number of lands with the basic land type as dictated by the card. Some effect is gained from this. Not a good mechanic."
  Threshold,ability_word,Nimble Mongoose,Cards with threshold gain some effect when you have 7 or more cards in the graveyard.
  Undergrowth,ability_word,Kraul Foragers,Cards with undergrowth have effects dependent on the amount of creatures in your graveyard.

# Added by Claude, 2026-10-22 (user: "add missing keywords to reference"). The table above is the user's document and is unchanged. These entries come from the AI lab's list of Forge keywords missing from it plus general rules knowledge, not from the user's document; examples are cards from the local Scryfall data that carry the keyword. Check against the Forge script / Oracle line before relying on a summary. Storied is taken from the reminder text on Bombur, Gentle Dreamer's Oracle line.
keywords_added[13]{name,kind,example,summary,source}:
  Hexproof,keyword,Soul of the Rapids,Cannot be the target of spells or abilities an opponent controls. Its controller can still target it.,added_by_claude
  Infect,keyword,Phyrexian Juggernaut,Damage it deals to creatures is dealt as -1/-1 counters and damage to players gives poison counters instead of life loss. A player with 10 poison counters loses.,added_by_claude
  Toxic,keyword,Tyrranax Atrocity,Written as Toxic X. When the creature deals combat damage to a player that player also gets X poison counters in addition to the normal damage.,added_by_claude
  Warp,keyword,Starbreach Whale,Written as Warp [cost]. Cast the card from hand for its warp cost; exile it at the next end step and it can be cast again from exile on a later turn.,added_by_claude
  Plot,keyword,Unscrupulous Contractor,Written as Plot [cost]. Pay the plot cost at sorcery timing to exile the card; on a later turn cast it from exile for free at sorcery timing.,added_by_claude
  Saddle,keyword,Caustic Bronco,Written as Saddle X on Mounts. At sorcery timing tap other creatures with total power X or more; the Mount becomes saddled until end of turn and may use its saddled abilities.,added_by_claude
  Station,keyword,Wedgelight Rammer,Written as Station on Spacecraft. Tap another creature you control to put charge counters equal to its power on the Spacecraft; at certain counter totals it gains abilities and becomes a creature.,added_by_claude
  Chapter,keyword,,Chapter abilities are the numbered abilities on a Saga. A lore counter is added each turn after the first main phase draw step and each chapter triggers when counters reach its number; the Saga is sacrificed after the last chapter.,added_by_claude
  Class,keyword,,Class enchantments have levels. Pay each level's cost at sorcery timing in order to unlock that level's ability; levels are permanent while the Class stays on the battlefield.,added_by_claude
  Partner,keyword,Lore Weaver,Commander rule keyword. Two commanders that both have partner can be the same deck's commanders. Variants (Partner with, Friends forever, Choose a Background) restrict which pairs are legal.,added_by_claude
  Devoid,keyword,Void Grafter,The card is colorless even though its mana cost has colored symbols.,added_by_claude
  Choose a Background,keyword,Halsin Emerald Archdruid,Commander rule keyword. Lets the commander have a Background enchantment as a second commander.,added_by_claude
  Storied,keyword,Balin Loremaster,If you control three or more artifacts / legendary permanents / Sagas (any mix) you have an enduring story for the rest of the game; some Storied cards act differently once you do.,forge_oracle_reminder_text

# Added from the Comprehensive Rules, 2026-10-22 (user: add the CR-only keywords). Source is rules 701 (keyword actions) and 702 (keyword abilities) in tools/agents/reference/MTG_COMP_RULES_20260807.txt; summary = the first lines of the rule text, trimmed to 300 characters; reminder_text and example come from KEYWORD_REMINDER_TEXT.toon (empty = no card prints reminder text). Forge K: spelling not checked for these.
keywords_from_rules[104]{name,kind,rule,summary,reminder_text,example}:
  Create,action,701.7,"To create one or more tokens with certain characteristics, put the specified number of tokens with the specified characteristics onto the battlefield.","",""
  Destroy,action,701.8,"To destroy a permanent, move it from the battlefield to its owner's graveyard.","",""
  Discard,action,701.9,"To discard a card, move it from its owner's hand to that player's graveyard.","",""
  Double,action,701.10,Doubling a creature's power and/or toughness creates a continuous effect. This effect modifies that creature's power and/or toughness but doesn't set those characteristics to a specific value. See rule 613.4c.,"",""
  Triple,action,701.11,Tripling a creature's power and/or toughness creates a continuous effect. This effect modifies that creature's power and/or toughness but doesn't set those characteristics to a specific value. See rule 613.4c.,"",""
  Exchange,action,701.12,"A spell or ability may instruct players to exchange something (for example, life totals or control of two permanents) as part of its resolution. When such a spell or ability resolves, if the entire exchange can't be completed, no part of the exchange occurs. Example: If a spell attempts to exchange ","",""
  Exile,action,701.13,"To exile an object, move it to the exile zone from wherever it is. See rule 406, \"Exile.\"","",""
  Fight,action,701.14,A spell or ability may instruct a creature to fight another creature or it may instruct two creatures to fight each other. Each of those creatures deals damage equal to its power to the other creature.,"",""
  Goad,action,701.15,"Certain spells and abilities can goad a creature. Until the next turn of the controller of that spell or ability, that creature is goaded.","",""
  Mill,action,701.17,"For a player to mill a number of cards, that player puts that many cards from the top of their library into their graveyard.","",""
  Play,action,701.18,"To play a land means to put it onto the battlefield from the zone it's in (usually the hand). A player may play a land if they have priority, it's the main phase of their turn, the stack is empty, and they haven't played a land this turn. Playing a land is a special action (see rule 116), so it does","",""
  Reveal,action,701.20,"To reveal a card, show that card to all players for a brief time. If an effect causes a card to be revealed, it remains revealed for as long as necessary to complete the parts of the effect that card is relevant to. If the cost to cast a spell or activate an ability includes revealing a card, or if ","",""
  Search,action,701.23,"To search for a card in a zone, look at all cards in that zone (even if it's a hidden zone) and find a card that matches the given description.","",""
  Shuffle,action,701.24,"To shuffle a library or a face-down pile of cards, randomize the cards within it so that no player knows their order.","",""
  Planeswalk,action,701.31,"A player may planeswalk only during a Planechase game. Only the planar controller may planeswalk. See rule 901, \"Planechase.\"","",""
  Set in Motion,action,701.32,"Only a scheme card may be set in motion, and only during an Archenemy game. Only the archenemy may set a scheme card in motion. See rule 314, \"Schemes,\" and rule 904, \"Archenemy.\"","",""
  Abandon,action,701.33,"Only a face-up ongoing scheme card may be abandoned, and only during an Archenemy game. See rule 314, \"Schemes,\" and rule 904, \"Archenemy.\"","",""
  Vote,action,701.38,"Some spells and abilities instruct players to vote for one choice from a list of options to determine some aspect of the effect of that spell or ability. To vote, each player, starting with a specified player and proceeding in turn order, chooses one of those choices.","",""
  Assemble,action,701.45,"Assemble is a keyword action in the Unstable set that puts Contraptions onto the battlefield. Outside of silver-bordered cards, only one card (Steamflogger Boss) refers to assembling a Contraption. Cards and mechanics from the Unstable set aren't included in these rules. See the Unstable FAQ for mor","",""
  Amass,action,701.47,"To amass [subtype] N means \"If you don't control an Army creature, create a 0/0 black [subtype] Army creature token. Choose an Army creature you control. Put N +1/+1 counters on that creature. If it isn't a [subtype], it becomes a [subtype] in addition to its other types.\"","",""
  Learn,action,701.48,"\"Learn\" means \"You may discard a card. If you do, draw a card. If you didn't discard a card, you may reveal a Lesson card you own from outside the game and put it into your hand.\"","",""
  Venture into the Dungeon,action,701.49,"If a player is instructed to venture into the dungeon while they don't own a dungeon card in the command zone, they choose a dungeon card they own from outside the game and put it into the command zone. They put their venture marker on the topmost room. See rule 309, \"Dungeons.\"","",""
  Open an Attraction,action,701.51,"A player may open an Attraction only during a game in which that player is playing with an Attraction deck (see rule 717, \"Attraction Cards\").","",""
  Roll to Visit Your Attractions,action,701.52,"To roll to visit your Attractions, roll a six-sided die. Then if you control one or more Attractions with a number lit up that is equal to that result, each of those Attractions has been \"visited\" and its visit ability triggers. See rule 717, \"Attraction Cards,\" and rule 702.159, \"Visit.\"","",""
  Incubate,action,701.53,"To incubate N, create an Incubator token that enters the battlefield with N +1/+1 counters on it. See rule 111.10i.","",""
  The Ring Tempts You,action,701.54,"Certain spells and abilities have the text \"the Ring tempts you.\" Each time the Ring tempts you, choose a creature you control. That creature becomes your Ring-bearer until another creature becomes your Ring-bearer or another player gains control of it.","",""
  Face a Villainous Choice,action,701.55,"\"[A player] faces a villainous choice — [option A], or [option B]\" means \"[A player] chooses [option A] or [option B]. Then all actions in the chosen option are performed.\"","",""
  Discover,action,701.57,"\"Discover N\" means \"Exile cards from the top of your library until you exile a nonland card with mana value N or less. You may cast that card without paying its mana cost if the resulting spell's mana value is less than or equal to N. If you don't cast it, put that card into your hand. Put the remai","",""
  Cloak,action,701.58,"To cloak a card, turn it face down. It becomes a 2/2 face-down creature card with ward {2}, no name, no subtypes, and no mana cost. Put that card onto the battlefield face down. That permanent is a cloaked permanent for as long as it remains face down. The effect defining its characteristics works w","",""
  Suspect,action,701.60,Certain spells and abilities instruct a player to suspect a creature. That creature becomes suspected until it leaves the battlefield or until a spell or ability causes it to no longer be suspected.,"",""
  Forage,action,701.61,"To forage means \"Exile three cards from your graveyard or sacrifice a Food.\"","",""
  Manifest Dread,action,701.62,"\"Manifest dread\" means \"Look at the top two cards of your library. Manifest one of them, then put the cards you looked at that were not manifested this way into your graveyard.\" See rule 701.40, \"Manifest.\"","",""
  Endure,action,701.63,"Certain abilities instruct a permanent to endure N. To do so, that permanent's controller creates an N/N white Spirit creature token unless they put N +1/+1 counters on that permanent.","",""
  Harness,action,701.64,"\"Harness [this permanent]\" means \"If this permanent isn't harnessed, it becomes harnessed.\"","",""
  Airbend,action,701.65,"Certain spells and abilities instruct a player to airbend one or more permanents and/or spells. To do so, that player exiles those objects. For each card exiled this way, for as long as it remains exiled, its owner may cast it by paying {2} rather than paying its mana cost.","",""
  Earthbend,action,701.66,"\"Earthbend N\" means \"Target land you control becomes a 0/0 land creature with haste in addition to its other types. Put N +1/+1 counters on it. When that land dies or is put into exile, return it to the battlefield tapped under your control.\"","",""
  Waterbend,action,701.67,"\"Waterbend [cost]\" means \"Pay [cost]. For each generic mana in that cost, you may tap an untapped artifact or creature you control rather than pay that mana.\"","",""
  Blight,action,701.68,"To \"blight N\" means to put N -1/-1 counters on a creature you control.","",""
  Heal,action,701.69,"To heal damage already dealt to a permanent, remove that marked damage from that permanent. If an effect states that damage already dealt to a permanent \"is healed,\" that permanent's controller removes all marked damage from that permanent.","",""
  Vanishing,keyword,702.63,"Vanishing is a keyword that represents three abilities. \"Vanishing N\" means \"This permanent enters with N time counters on it,\" \"At the beginning of your upkeep, if this permanent has a time counter on it, remove a time counter from it,\" and \"When the last time counter is removed from this permanent","This creature enters with three time counters on it. At the beginning of your upkeep, remove a time counter from it. When the last is removed, sacrifice it.",Chronozoa
  Fortify,keyword,702.67,"Fortify is an activated ability of Fortification cards. \"Fortify [cost]\" means \"[Cost]: Attach this Fortification to target land you control. Activate only as a sorcery.\"",{C}: Attach to target land you control. Fortify only as a sorcery.,C.A.M.P.
  Umbra Armor,keyword,702.89,"Umbra armor is a static ability that appears on some Auras. \"Umbra armor\" means \"If enchanted permanent would be destroyed, instead remove all damage marked on it and destroy this Aura.\"","If enchanted creature would be destroyed, instead remove all damage from it and destroy this Aura.",Bear Umbra
  Fuse,keyword,702.102,"Fuse is a static ability found on some split cards (see rule 709, \"Split Cards\") that applies while the card with fuse is in a player's hand. If a player casts a split card with fuse from their hand, the player may choose to cast both halves of that split card rather than choose one half. This choic",You may cast one or both halves of this card from your hand.,Beck
  Dethrone,keyword,702.105,"Dethrone is a triggered ability. \"Dethrone\" means \"Whenever this creature attacks the player with the most life or tied for most life, put a +1/+1 counter on this creature.\"","Whenever this creature attacks the player with the most life or tied for most life, put a +N/+N counter on it.","Marchesa, the Black Rose"
  Hidden Agenda,keyword,702.106,"Hidden agenda is a static ability that functions as a conspiracy card with hidden agenda is put into the command zone. \"Hidden agenda\" means \"As you put this conspiracy card into the command zone, turn it face down and secretly choose a card name.\"",Start the game with this conspiracy face down in the command zone and secretly choose a card name. You may turn this conspiracy face up any time and reveal that name.,Brago's Favor
  Outlast,keyword,702.107,"Outlast is an activated ability. \"Outlast [cost]\" means \"[Cost], {T}: Put a +1/+1 counter on this creature. Activate only as a sorcery.\"","{C}, {C}: Put a +N/+N counter on this creature. Outlast only as a sorcery.",Mer-Ek Nightblade
  Awaken,keyword,702.113,"Awaken appears on some instants and sorceries. It represents two abilities: a static ability that functions while the spell with awaken is on the stack and a spell ability. \"Awaken N— [cost]\" means \"You may pay [cost] rather than pay this spell's mana cost as you cast this spell\" and \"If this spell'","If you cast this spell for {C}{C}, also put four +N/+N counters on target land you control and it becomes a N/N Elemental creature with haste. It's still a land.",Boiling Earth
  Ingest,keyword,702.115,"Ingest is a triggered ability. \"Ingest\" means \"Whenever this creature deals combat damage to a player, that player exiles the top card of their library.\"","Whenever this creature deals combat damage to a player, that player exiles the top card of their library.",Benthic Infiltrator
  Myriad,keyword,702.116,"Myriad is a triggered ability that may also create a delayed triggered ability. \"Myriad\" means \"Whenever this creature attacks, for each opponent other than defending player, you may create a token that's a copy of this creature that's tapped and attacking that player or a planeswalker they control.","Whenever this creature attacks, for each opponent other than defending player, you may create a token copy that's tapped and attacking that player or a planeswalker they control. Exile the tokens at end of combat.",Banshee of the Dread Choir
  Surge,keyword,702.117,"Surge is a static ability that functions while the spell with surge is on the stack. \"Surge [cost]\" means \"You may pay [cost] rather than pay this spell's mana cost as you cast this spell if you or one of your teammates has cast another spell this turn.\" Casting a spell for its surge cost follows th",You may cast this spell for its surge cost if you or a teammate has cast another spell this turn.,Boulder Salvo
  Skulk,keyword,702.118,Skulk is an evasion ability.,This creature can't be blocked by creatures with greater power.,Ingenious Prodigy
  Escalate,keyword,702.120,"Escalate is a static ability of modal spells (see rule 700.2) that functions while the spell with escalate is on the stack. \"Escalate [cost]\" means \"For each mode you choose beyond the first as you cast this spell, you pay an additional [cost].\" Paying a spell's escalate cost follows the rules for p",Pay this cost for each mode chosen beyond the first.,Blessed Alliance
  Melee,keyword,702.121,"Melee is a triggered ability. \"Melee\" means \"Whenever this creature attacks, it gets +1/+1 until end of turn for each opponent you attacked with a creature this combat.\"","Whenever this creature attacks, it gets +N/+N until end of turn for each opponent you attacked this combat.",Wings of the Guard
  Fabricate,keyword,702.123,"Fabricate is a triggered ability. \"Fabricate N\" means \"When this permanent enters, you may put N +1/+1 counters on it. If you don't, create N 1/1 colorless Servo artifact creature tokens.\"","When this creature enters, put a +N/+N counter on it or create a N/N colorless Servo artifact creature token.",Iron League Steed
  Undaunted,keyword,702.125,"Undaunted is a static ability that functions while the spell with undaunted is on the stack. Undaunted means \"This spell costs {1} less to cast for each opponent you have.\"",This spell costs {C} less to cast for each opponent.,Curtains' Call
  Improvise,keyword,702.126,"Improvise is a static ability that functions while the spell with improvise is on the stack. \"Improvise\" means \"For each generic mana in this spell's total cost, you may tap an untapped artifact you control rather than pay that mana.\"",Your artifacts can help cast this spell. Each artifact you tap after you're done activating mana abilities pays for {C}.,Barricade Breaker
  Eternalize,keyword,702.129,"Eternalize is an activated ability that functions while the card with eternalize is in a graveyard. \"Eternalize [cost]\" means \"[Cost], Exile this card from your graveyard: Create a token that's a copy of this card, except it's black, it's 4/4, it has no mana cost, and it's a Zombie in addition to it","{C}{C}{C}, Exile this card from your graveyard: Create a token that's a copy of it, except it's a N/N black Zombie Human Shaman with no mana cost. Eternalize only as a sorcery.",Timeless Witness
  Afflict,keyword,702.130,"Afflict is a triggered ability. \"Afflict N\" means \"Whenever this creature becomes blocked, defending player loses N life.\"","Whenever this creature becomes blocked, defending player loses N life.",Wildfire Eternal
  Ascend,keyword,702.131,"Ascend on an instant or sorcery spell represents a spell ability. It means \"If you control ten or more permanents and you don't have the city's blessing, you get the city's blessing for the rest of the game.\"","If you control ten or more permanents, you get the city's blessing for the rest of the game.",Illustrious Wanderglyph
  Assist,keyword,702.132,"Assist is a static ability that modifies the rules of paying for the spell with assist (see rules 601.2g-h). If the total cost to cast a spell with assist includes a generic mana component, before you activate mana abilities while casting it, you may choose another player. That player has a chance t",Another player can pay up to {C} of this spell's cost.,Bloodborn Scoundrels
  Companion,keyword,702.139,"Companion is a keyword ability that functions outside the game. It's written as \"Companion—[Condition].\" Before the game begins, you may reveal one card you own from outside the game with a companion ability whose condition is fulfilled by your starting deck. (See rule 103.2b.) Once during the game,","",""
  Encore,keyword,702.141,"Encore is an activated ability that functions while the card with encore is in a graveyard. \"Encore [cost]\" means \"[Cost], Exile this card from your graveyard: For each opponent, create a token that's a copy of this card that attacks that opponent this turn if able. The tokens gain haste. Sacrifice ","{C}{C}{C}, Exile this card from your graveyard: For each opponent, create a token copy that attacks that opponent this turn if able. They gain haste. Sacrifice them at the beginning of the next end step. Activate only as a sorcery.",Belonging
  Boast,keyword,702.142,"Boast is a keyword that adds additional rules to the activated ability that follows it. \"Boast — [Cost]: [Effect]\" means \"[Cost]: [Effect]. Activate only if this creature attacked this turn and only once each turn.\"","",""
  Demonstrate,keyword,702.144,"Demonstrate is a triggered ability. \"Demonstrate\" means \"When you cast this spell, you may copy it and you may choose new targets for the copy. If you copy the spell, choose an opponent. That player copies the spell and may choose new targets for that copy.\"","When you cast this spell, you may copy it. If you do, choose an opponent to also copy it. Players may choose new targets for their copies.",Transforming Flourish
  Decayed,keyword,702.147,"Decayed represents a static ability and a triggered ability. \"Decayed\" means \"This creature can't block\" and \"When this creature attacks, sacrifice it at end of combat.\"","This creature can't block. When it attacks, sacrifice it at end of combat.",Rot-Curse Rakshasa
  Cleave,keyword,702.148,"Cleave is a keyword that represents two static abilities that function while a spell with cleave is on the stack. \"Cleave [cost]\" means \"You may cast this spell by paying [cost] rather than paying its mana cost\" and \"If this spell's cleave cost was paid, change its text by removing all text found wi","You may cast this spell for its cleave cost. If you do, remove the words in square brackets.",Inspired Idea
  Training,keyword,702.149,"Training is a triggered ability. \"Training\" means \"Whenever this creature and at least one other creature with power greater than this creature's power attack, put a +1/+1 counter on this creature.\"","Whenever this creature attacks with another creature with greater power, put a +N/+N counter on this creature.",Jenny Flint
  Compleated,keyword,702.150,"Compleated is a static ability found on some planeswalker cards. Compleated means \"If this permanent would enter with one or more loyalty counters on it and the player who cast it chose to pay life for any part of its cost represented by Phyrexian mana symbols, it instead enters the battlefield with","{C} can be paid with {C}, {C}, or N life. If life was paid, this planeswalker enters with two fewer loyalty counters.","Tamiyo, Compleated Sage"
  Enlist,keyword,702.154,"Enlist represents a static ability and a triggered ability. Enlist means \"As this creature attacks, you may tap up to one untapped creature you control that you didn't choose to attack with and that either has haste or has been under your control continuously since this turn began. When you do, this","As this creature attacks, you may tap a nonattacking creature you control without summoning sickness. When you do, add its power to this creature's until end of turn.",Benalish Faithbonder
  Read Ahead,keyword,702.155,"Read ahead is a keyword found on some Saga cards. \"Read ahead\" means \"Chapter abilities of this Saga can't trigger the turn it entered the battlefield unless it has exactly the number of lore counters on it specified in the chapter symbol of that ability.\" See rule 714, \"Saga Cards.\"",Choose a chapter and start with that many lore counters. Add one after your draw step. Skipped chapters don't trigger. Sacrifice after III.,Braids's Frightful Return
  Ravenous,keyword,702.156,"Ravenous is a keyword found on some creature cards with {X} in their mana cost. Ravenous represents both a replacement effect and a triggered ability. \"Ravenous\" means \"This permanent enters with X +1/+1 counters on it\" and \"When this permanent enters, if X is 5 or more, draw a card.\" See rule 107.3","This creature enters with X +N/+N counters on it. If X is N or more, draw a card when it enters.",Broodlord
  Squad,keyword,702.157,"Squad is a keyword that represents two linked abilities. The first is a static ability that functions while the creature spell with squad is on the stack. The second is a triggered ability that functions when the creature with squad enters the battlefield. \"Squad [cost]\" means \"As an additional cost","As an additional cost to cast this spell, you may pay {C} any number of times. When this creature enters, create that many tokens that are copies of it.",Wasteland Raider
  Space Sculptor,keyword,702.158,One card (Space Beleren) has the space sculptor ability. This keyword ability causes creatures to gain sector designations.,"Space Beleren divides the battlefield into alpha, beta, and gamma sectors. If a creature isn't assigned to a sector, its controller assigns it to one. Opponents assign first.",Space Beleren
  Visit,keyword,702.159,"Visit is a keyword ability found on Attraction cards (see rule 717). \"Visit — [Effect]\" means \"Whenever you roll to visit your Attractions, if the result is equal to a number that is lit up on this Attraction, [effect].\" See rule 701.52, \"Roll to Visit Your Attractions.\"","",""
  Prototype,keyword,702.160,"Prototype is a static ability that appears on prototype cards that have a secondary set of power, toughness, and mana cost characteristics. A player who casts a spell with prototype can choose to cast that card \"prototyped.\" If they do, the alternative set of its power, toughness, and mana cost char","You may cast this spell with different mana cost, color, and size. It keeps its abilities and types.",Boulderbranch Golem
  Living Metal,keyword,702.161,"Living metal is a keyword ability found on some Vehicles. \"Living metal\" means \"During your turn, this permanent is an artifact creature in addition to its other types.\"","",""
  More Than Meets the Eye,keyword,702.162,"More Than Meets the Eye represents a static ability that functions in any zone from which the spell may be cast. \"More Than Meets the Eye [cost]\" means \"You may cast this card converted by paying [cost] rather than its mana cost.\" Casting a spell using its More Than Meets the Eye ability follows the",You may cast this card converted for {C}{C}.,"Blitzwing, Cruel Tormentor"
  For Mirrodin!,keyword,702.163,"For Mirrodin! is a triggered ability. \"For Mirrodin!\" means \"When this Equipment enters, create a 2/2 red Rebel creature token, then attach this Equipment to it.\"","When this Equipment enters, create a N/N red Rebel creature token, then attach this to it.",Bladehold War-Whip
  Backup,keyword,702.165,"Backup is a triggered ability. \"Backup N\" means \"When this creature enters, put N +1/+1 counters on target creature. If that's another creature, it also gains the non-backup abilities of this creature printed below this one until end of turn.\" Cards with backup have one or more abilities printed aft","When this creature enters, put a +N/+N counter on target creature. If that's another creature, it gains the following ability until end of turn.","Bright-Palm, Soul Awakener"
  Bargain,keyword,702.166,"Bargain is a static ability that functions while the spell with bargain is on the stack. \"Bargain\" means \"As an additional cost to cast this spell, you may sacrifice an artifact, enchantment, or token.\" Paying a spell's bargain cost follows the rules for paying additional costs in rules 601.2b and 6","You may sacrifice an artifact, enchantment, or token as you cast this spell.",Brave the Wilds
  Craft,keyword,702.167,"Craft represents an activated ability. It is written as \"Craft with [materials] [cost],\" where [materials] is a description of one or more objects. It means \"[Cost], Exile this permanent, Exile [materials] from among permanents you control and/or cards in your graveyard: Return this card to the batt","{C}{C}{C}, Exile this artifact, Exile another artifact you control or an artifact card from your graveyard: Return this card transformed under its owner's control. Craft only as a sorcery.",Inverted Iceberg
  Disguise,keyword,702.168,"Disguise is a static ability that functions in any zone from which you could play the card it's on, and the disguise effect works any time the card is face down. \"Disguise [cost]\" means \"You may cast this card as a 2/2 face-down creature with ward {2}, no name, no subtypes, and no mana cost by payin",You may cast this card face down for {C} as a N/N creature with ward {C}. Turn it face up any time for its disguise cost.,Bolrac-Clan Basher
  Solved,keyword,702.169,"Solved is a keyword ability found on Case cards. See rule 719, \"Case Cards.\" \"Solved\" is followed by ability text. Together, they represent a static ability, a triggered ability, or an activated ability.","",""
  Spree,keyword,702.172,"Spree is a static ability found on some modal spells (see rule 700.2) that applies while the spell on the stack. Spree means \"Choose one or more modes. As an additional cost to cast this spell, pay the costs associated with those modes.\"",Choose one or more additional costs.,Insatiable Avarice
  Freerunning,keyword,702.173,"Freerunning is a static ability that functions on the stack. \"Freerunning [cost]\" means \"You may pay [cost] rather than pay this spell's mana cost if a player was dealt combat damage this turn by a creature that, at the time it dealt that damage, was an Assassin creature or a commander under your co",You may cast this spell for its freerunning cost if you dealt combat damage to a player this turn with an Assassin or commander.,Brotherhood Ambushers
  Gift,keyword,702.174,"Gift is a keyword that represents two abilities. It is written \"Gift a [something].\" The first ability is a static ability that functions while the card with gift is on the stack, and the second is either an ability that functions while the card with gift is on the stack or a triggered ability that ","You may promise an opponent a gift as you cast this spell. If you do, they draw a card before its other effects.",Wear Down
  Offspring,keyword,702.175,"Offspring represents two abilities. \"Offspring [cost]\" means \"You may pay an additional [cost] as you cast this spell\" and \"When this permanent enters, if its offspring cost was paid, create a token that's a copy of it, except it's 1/1.\"","You may pay an additional {C} as you cast this spell. If you do, when this creature enters, create a N/N token copy of it.",Bushy Bodyguard
  Impending,keyword,702.176,Impending is a keyword that represents four abilities. The first is a static ability that functions while the spell with impending is on the stack. The second is static ability that creates a replacement effect that may apply to the permanent with impending as it enters the battlefield from the stac,"If you cast this spell for its impending cost, it enters with four time counters and isn't a creature until the last is removed. At the beginning of your end step, remove a time counter from it.",Overlord of the Floodpits
  Exhaust,keyword,702.177,"Exhaust is a keyword that adds additional rules to the activated ability that follows it. \"Exhaust — [Cost]: [Effect]\" means \"[Cost]: [Effect]. Activate only once.\"","",""
  Max Speed,keyword,702.178,"A max speed ability is a static ability. \"Max speed — [Ability]\" means \"As long as your speed is 4, this object has ‘[Ability].'\" See rule 702.179, \"Start Your Engines!\" 702.178b If an ability granted by a max speed ability states which zones it functions from, the max speed ability that grants that","",""
  Start Your Engines!,keyword,702.179,"Start your engines! is a static ability. If a player controls a permanent with start your engines! and that player has no speed, their speed becomes 1. This is a state-based action. See rule 704.","If you have no speed, it starts at N. It increases once on each of your turns when an opponent loses life. Max speed is N.",Burnout Bashtronaut
  Harmonize,keyword,702.180,"Harmonize represents three static abilities: one that functions while the card is in a player's graveyard and two that function while the spell with harmonize is on the stack. \"Harmonize [cost]\" means \"You may cast this card from your graveyard by paying [cost] and tapping up to one untapped creatur","You may cast this card from your graveyard for its harmonize cost. You may tap a creature you control to reduce that cost by {C}, where X is its power. Then exile this spell.",Wild Ride
  Mobilize,keyword,702.181,"Mobilize is a triggered ability. \"Mobilize N\" means \"Whenever this creature attacks, create N 1/1 red Warrior creature tokens. Those tokens enter tapped and attacking. Sacrifice them at the beginning of the next end step.\"","Whenever this creature attacks, create a tapped and attacking N/N red Warrior creature token. Sacrifice it at the beginning of the next end step.",Venerated Stormsinger
  Job Select,keyword,702.182,"Job select is a triggered ability. \"Job select\" means \"When this Equipment enters, create a 1/1 colorless Hero creature token, then attach this Equipment to it.\"","When this Equipment enters, create a N/N colorless Hero creature token, then attach this to it.",Black Mage's Rod
  Tiered,keyword,702.183,"Tiered is a static ability found on some modal spells (see rule 700.2) that applies while the spell is on the stack. Tiered means \"Choose one. As an additional cost to cast this spell, pay the cost associated with that mode.\" 702.184. Station",Choose one additional cost.,Ice Magic
  ∞ (Infinity),keyword,702.186,"∞ (the mathematical symbol for infinity) is a keyword found on Infinity cards. \"∞\" is followed by ability text. Together, they represent a static ability.","",""
  Mayhem,keyword,702.187,Mayhem is a static ability that functions while the card with mayhem is in a player's graveyard.,You may cast this card from your graveyard for {C}{C} if you discarded it this turn. Timing rules still apply.,Prison Break
  Web-slinging,keyword,702.188,"Web-slinging is a static ability that functions while the spell with web-slinging is on the stack. \"Web-slinging [cost]\" means \"You may cast this spell by paying [cost] and returning a tapped creature you control to its owner's hand rather than paying its mana cost.\" Casting a spell using its web-sl",You may cast this spell for {C}{C} if you also return a tapped creature you control to its owner's hand.,Spider-UK
  Firebending,keyword,702.189,"Firebending is a triggered ability. \"Firebending N\" means \"Whenever this creature attacks, add N {R}. Until end of combat, you don't lose this mana as steps and phases end.\"","Whenever this creature attacks, add {C}. This mana lasts until end of combat.",Boiling Rock Rioter
  Sneak,keyword,702.190,"Sneak is a keyword that represents a static ability that functions while the spell with sneak is on the stack. \"Sneak [cost]\" means \"Any time you could cast an instant during your declare blockers step, you may cast this spell by paying [cost] and returning an unblocked creature you control to its o",You may cast this spell for {C}{C} if you also return an unblocked attacker you control to hand during the declare blockers step.,Michelangelo's Technique
  Increment,keyword,702.191,"Increment is a triggered ability. \"Increment\" means \"Whenever you cast a spell, if this permanent is a creature and the amount of mana spent to cast that spell is greater than this creature's power or this creature's toughness, put a +1/+1 counter on this creature.\"","Whenever you cast a spell, if the amount of mana you spent is greater than this creature's power or toughness, put a +N/+N counter on this creature.","Berta, Wise Extrapolator"
  Paradigm,keyword,702.192,"Paradigm represents two spell abilities, one of which creates a delayed triggered ability. Paradigm means \"If this is the first time a spell you control with this spell's name has resolved this game, at the beginning of each of your precombat main phases for the rest of the game, create a copy of th","Then exile this spell. After you first resolve a spell with this name, you may cast a copy of it from exile without paying its mana cost at the beginning of each of your first main phases.",Improvisation Capstone
  Power-up,keyword,702.193,"Power-up is a keyword that adds additional rules to the activated ability that follows it. \"Power-up — [Cost]: [Effect]\" means \"[Cost]: [Effect]. If this permanent entered this turn, this ability's cost is reduced by this permanent's mana cost. Activate this ability only once.\"","",""
  Teamwork,keyword,702.194,"Teamwork represents a static ability that functions while the spell with teamwork is on the stack. \"Teamwork N\" means \"As an additional cost to cast this spell, you may tap any number of creatures you control with total power N or more.\" Paying a spell's teamwork cost follows the rules for paying ad","As an additional cost to cast this spell, you may tap any number of creatures you control with total power N or more.",Beast Mode
